WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:02.960
- [Narrator] This is a
Bitcoin mine hidden deep

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.745
in the mountains of Sichuan in China.

00:00:05.745 --> 00:00:09.970
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:10.803
- [Narrator] And its rival

00:00:10.803 --> 00:00:12.530
is on the other side of the planet

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.660
at a former factory

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.890
that used to make denim for Levi's.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.850
- You see the transformers
lined up on the outside.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.840
We have a lot of megawatts.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.120
- These two miners make money

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.110
by providing the massive computing power

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:24.430
that's required to process

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.840
and record a high volume of
cryptocurrency transactions.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.464
Business was soaring as Bitcoin
hit new highs in early 2021.

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:33.297
- It's hard to sleep.

00:00:33.297 --> 00:00:34.921
You go to bed at night and
you wake up and you look

00:00:34.921 --> 00:00:37.040
and you go, "Holy crap, it's still up.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.130
- [Narrator] Last year,
China controlled 70%

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.590
of the global processing power

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.380
that runs the Bitcoin network

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:43.590
and that means the majority

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.950
of the cryptocurrency's
global transactions

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.920
are routed through
these computers in China

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.703
and recorded by miners here.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.580
So a group of US miners
is raising hundreds

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.820
of millions of dollars
to win a larger share

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:58.040
of Bitcoin's processing power.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.280
- When capitalism in the
States decides it wants

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:02.140
to get into market, get into an industry,

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:03.940
it moves heavy capital there.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:05.530
- [Narrator] They say
their work is also meant

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.750
to protect Bitcoin.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.880
Industry insiders say
the Chinese government

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.840
has already cracked down on
some crypto entrepreneurs

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.120
and could potentially
disrupt global trading

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.610
by asking miners in China

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.900
to block certain users
from making transactions.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.540
- It's better for
cryptocurrency to be spread

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.373
around the globe.

00:01:22.373 --> 00:01:23.810
So that Bitcoin cannot be manipulated

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.490
by any single government.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.010
- I think there will be competition.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.000
There's more and more human resources,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.710
technology resources that we're putting

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.430
into this particular new segment.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:34.930
- [Narrator] The battle
over Bitcoin mining

00:01:34.930 --> 00:01:37.280
will decide who controls
the infrastructure

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.830
that powers the cryptocurrency.

00:01:43.053 --> 00:01:46.970
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.360
- [Narrator] Yulong Liu started mining

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.540
during the previous Bitcoin rally in 2017.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.380
And this is one of the sites he works with

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.410
that has mined about 8,000 Bitcoins

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.060
over the past three years,

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.740
generating about $28 million in revenue

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.083
over that time period.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:07.720
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.330
- [Narrator] Miners
need cheap electricity,

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:11.900
which is abundant in some
parts of China thanks

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.600
to dams and coal power plants

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.460
that were built by the
state in the past decade.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.670
That electricity then powers fast machines

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.160
that are necessary to
solve mathematical problems

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.150
in order to eventually mint new coins.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.950
China is home to the vast majority

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.550
of mining equipment production

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.210
and so miners like Liu
always have speedy access

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.510
to the best technology,

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.213
like this cooling system.

00:02:33.213 --> 00:02:37.130
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:42.584 --> 00:02:43.900
- [Narrator] But the
industry in China lives

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.190
with uncertainty.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.610
Liu asked to keep the location

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:49.380
of the site a secret because
he says he's not sure

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.480
if the government will crack down one day.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.610
While mining itself isn't illegal,

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:55.910
virtual currency trading

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.350
and crypto exchanges are banned in China

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.610
because they're seen as risky

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.833
to the country's financial system.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.640
In the past few months,

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:05.300
Bitcoin industry insiders have said

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.490
that Beijing accused some Chinese miners

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:08.550
of money laundering

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.250
and froze their credit cards,

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.770
making it difficult for
miners to pay operating costs.

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.440
The Chinese government did not respond

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.833
to a request for comment.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.360
So to help miners develop their business

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.970
despite the risks,

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:24.110
Liu offers loans so miners don't need

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.733
to go through Chinese banks.

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.360
His company Babel Finance
lends cryptocurrencies

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.140
to about 300 miners,

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.883
including the owners of this site.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.740
- So that they can purchase more equipment

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.480
at a lower cost

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.100
and then maintaining the machine itself,

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:42.060
including repairs.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:42.990
- [Narrator] And Chinese miners

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:46.350
are now facing growing
competition from overseas.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.680
- In the United States,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.270
we have massive infrastructure,

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.160
power infrastructure and
building infrastructure

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.400
that's already been built out

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.920
and we can convert facilities

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.163
into large data mining facilities.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.790
- [Narrator] Russell
Cann is an American miner

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.230
who scouts the US for abandoned factories

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.821
and converts them into mining facilities.

00:04:03.821 --> 00:04:04.990
His goal?

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:07.540
Raise cash to develop
industrial-scale mining

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:10.030
in the US where until a few years ago,

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:13.300
most miners ran small DIY operations.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.040
- [Xander] This is my
housing for my computers

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.573
so that the heat is vented outside.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:20.380
- [Narrator] So Core Scientific

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:22.290
has built a team with former executives

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.080
from Microsoft and Myspace

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.453
and put together an
ambitious business plan.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.050
- We have Ernst &amp; Young
audit the financials.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.640
We have a strong balance sheet.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.600
We check a lot of boxes
for institutional investors

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.160
that a Chinese miner does not check.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.250
- [Narrator] The strategy worked.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.270
In the past two years,

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.960
the company has raised $95 million

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.310
and secured a $20 million loan

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.250
to install mining rigs in facilities

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:49.270
including a former denim
factory in North Carolina

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:52.010
and a former carpet factory in Georgia.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:53.940
Core Scientific's power infrastructure

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.010
can handle the latest mining equipment,

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:58.560
which Cann says usually
consumes approximately

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.210
100 megawatt hours of
electricity to mine one Bitcoin.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:04.100
That's the same amount of electricity used

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:07.763
to watch television
continuously for about 98 years.

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.690
And tunnels that were once used

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:12.550
to cool the factory are now being used

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.550
to keep chips from overheating.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.790
- We've got the ability

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.520
to process 200,000
gallons of chilled water

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.290
through these pipes to
keep the temperature

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.343
in the building down.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.250
- [Narrator] Cann hopes all
this will help him offset

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.600
a long-running technological disadvantage.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.850
He was usually about four
months behind his Chinese rivals

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:33.200
when it came to accessing the latest rigs

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.363
and the price tag was
sometimes 50% more expensive.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.980
Others are using the
same playbook as Cann,

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.100
creating corporations
that attract the support

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:43.760
of institutional investors

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.083
who then help fund high-tech mining sites.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.640
Industry insiders and academics

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.750
who study mining say

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.090
that the US efforts can
be good for the future

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.631
of the cryptocurrency

00:05:53.631 --> 00:05:55.550
because the original goal of Bitcoin

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:56.850
was to create a currency

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:59.780
that couldn't be controlled by one entity.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:02.650
- The dream was that we
would reimagine finance

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:05.080
without gatekeepers and what did we get

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.200
after 11 years?

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:08.930
We got different kind of intermediaries.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.589
Now mostly nameless, mostly
under the covers in China.

00:06:12.589 --> 00:06:15.010
- [Narrator] Emin Gun Sirer
runs a blockchain startup

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:16.580
and is also an associate professor

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.063
at Cornell University.

00:06:18.063 --> 00:06:21.170
He studies the vulnerabilities
of cryptocurrencies

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:24.070
and says Beijing might
intervene in the market.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.480
- [Emin] This is an enormous issue.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.990
These miners, they could
receive injunctions

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.600
that compels them to act in a certain way.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.660
- [Narrator] One request he says

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.090
could be to ask miners
to exclude certain people

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:36.660
who want to spend or accept
Bitcoins in the network,

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.920
essentially blocking transactions.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:41.760
This is what Bitcoin
academics call censorship,

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.590
similar to how content and accounts

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.560
can be blocked on social
media platforms in China.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:48.763
- The Chinese government would say

00:06:48.763 --> 00:06:51.180
that the money at certain addresses

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.685
must not move and it
compels the Chinese miners

00:06:54.685 --> 00:06:57.140
to not include certain transactions

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:00.680
so they can selectively
sensor certain users

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.140
of a blockchain.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:03.840
- [Narrator] The Chinese
government did not respond

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.273
to a request for comment.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.500
Babel Finance says if miners in China

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:11.110
are asked by the government
to intervene in the network,

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.640
they would have to comply.

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:14.310
But that would slow down their operations

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:17.363
and eventually diminish their
global processing power.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.250
But US miners aren't
immune to facing scrutiny

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.370
from financial regulators at home

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.290
that have proposed plans

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.910
to hold the industry to
the same standards followed

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.143
by traditional financial institutions.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:32.980
The more immediate resistance

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.700
to US miners could come from
local communities concerned

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.673
about the environmental
impact of Bitcoin mining.

00:07:39.562 --> 00:07:41.340
- Bitcoin mining consumes enormous amounts

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:44.260
of energy so all energy
that goes to miners

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:46.520
is energy that's being directed away

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.490
from other more useful uses.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.720
- [Narrator] Cann says nearly
half of the electricity used

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.460
by Core Scientific comes
from carbon-free sources.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.020
Because China's miners aren't part

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:59.200
of a corporate structure like in the US,

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:01.300
Liu says that they can operate faster

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.460
and spend less on operating costs.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:05.847
- If you multiply the operational costs,

00:08:05.847 --> 00:08:07.836
China still has the advantage.

00:08:07.836 --> 00:08:11.950
China will be on the front
of the curve into the future.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:13.450
- 2021's all about expansion

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:14.910
and we've built infrastructure,

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.910
we've built the software,
we've built the team

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:18.623
to be a long-term player in this market.

00:08:18.623 --> 00:08:21.206
(upbeat music)

